---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { renderInlineMarkdown, renderMarkdown } from '../../../lib/markdown.js';
import { getStaticPage, getTaggedPages } from '../../../lib/pages.js';
import { cdnUrl } from '../../../lib/site.js';
const page = getStaticPage('docs/utilities/index');
const stripTags = html => html.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '');
const byTitle = (a, b) => String(a.data.title).toLowerCase().localeCompare(String(b.data.title).toLowerCase());
const styleUtilities = (await getTaggedPages('styleUtilities')).sort(byTitle);
const layoutUtilities = (await getTaggedPages('layoutUtilities')).sort(byTitle);
---

<Layout page={page}>
<p>
  <Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
  Preset CSS utility classes that let you efficiently customize styles and layouts for components and native elements alike.
  `)} />
</p>

<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
Instead of hand-writing the same CSS over and over, reach for a utility class and your theme takes care of the rest. CSS
utilities pull directly from your Web Awesome [theme](/docs/themes) and [design tokens](/docs/tokens), so colors,
typography, rounding, and spacing stay consistent with every component on the page. They're framework-agnostic, work on
any native HTML element, and can be combined freely.

## Using CSS Utilities

CSS utilities ship as part of \`webawesome.css\`, so if you're already including that stylesheet you don't need to import
anything else. Otherwise, follow these instructions to include the utilities stylesheet on its own.
`)} />

<wa-tab-group data-install-tabs="">
  <wa-tab panel="cdn"><wa-icon name="globe" variant="regular"></wa-icon> CDN</wa-tab>
  <wa-tab panel="npm"><wa-icon name="box-open" variant="regular"></wa-icon> npm</wa-tab>
  <wa-tab panel="self-hosted"><wa-icon name="arrow-down-to-line" variant="regular"></wa-icon> Self-Hosted</wa-tab>
  <wa-tab panel="hosted"><wa-icon name="rocket-launch" variant="regular"></wa-icon> Hosted Projects</wa-tab>

  <wa-tab-panel name="cdn">
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
Add the following stylesheet to the \`<head>\` section of your pages:

\`\`\`html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="${cdnUrl('styles/utilities.css')}">
\`\`\`
`)} />
  </wa-tab-panel>

  <wa-tab-panel name="npm">
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
After installing \`@awesome.me/webawesome\`, import the following stylesheet into your app:

\`\`\`js
import '@awesome.me/webawesome/dist/styles/utilities.css';
\`\`\`
`)} />
  </wa-tab-panel>

  <wa-tab-panel name="self-hosted">
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
Add the following stylesheet to the \`<head>\` section of your pages:

\`\`\`html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/dist/styles/utilities.css">
\`\`\`
`)} />
  </wa-tab-panel>

  <wa-tab-panel name="hosted">
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
If you're using a [hosted project](/workspaces), CSS utilities can be toggled on from your project settings.

1. Head over to your project's <wa-tag class="tag-ui" appearance="outlined"><wa-icon name="gear" variant="regular"></wa-icon> Settings</wa-tag>.
2. Next to <wa-tag class="tag-ui" appearance="outlined">Features</wa-tag>, select the <wa-tag class="tag-ui" appearance="outlined">CSS utilities</wa-tag> checkbox.
3. <wa-tag class="tag-ui" appearance="outlined">Save Changes</wa-tag> to immediately update anywhere you're using your project.
`)} />
  </wa-tab-panel>
</wa-tab-group>

<wa-divider></wa-divider>

<h2 class="modern-card-list-heading">Style Utilities</h2>
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
Preset rules for customizing colors, typography, rounding, and more &mdash; framework-agnostic and composable on any
element.
`)} />

<div class="modern-card-list">
  <section class="search-list-grid">
    {styleUtilities.map(item => (
          <a class="hover-grow hover-emphasize-border" href={item.url}>
            <wa-card>
              <span class="page-name">{item.data.title}</span>
              {item.data.description && (
                <p class="modern-card-summary" set:html={stripTags(renderInlineMarkdown(item.data.description))} />
              )}
            </wa-card>
          </a>
        ))}
  </section>
</div>

<h2 class="modern-card-list-heading">Layout Utilities</h2>
<Fragment set:html={renderMarkdown(`
Named layouts like [\`wa-stack\`](/docs/utilities/stack), [\`wa-cluster\`](/docs/utilities/cluster),
[\`wa-split\`](/docs/utilities/split), [\`wa-flank\`](/docs/utilities/flank), [\`wa-frame\`](/docs/utilities/frame), and
[\`wa-grid\`](/docs/utilities/grid) &mdash; plus property-level helpers for gap, alignment, and wrap &mdash; that organize
content responsively without custom CSS.
`)} />

<div class="modern-card-list">
  <section class="search-list-grid">
    {layoutUtilities.map(item => (
          <a class="hover-grow hover-emphasize-border" href={item.url}>
            <wa-card>
              <span class="page-name">{item.data.title}</span>
              {item.data.description && (
                <p class="modern-card-summary" set:html={stripTags(renderInlineMarkdown(item.data.description))} />
              )}
            </wa-card>
          </a>
        ))}
  </section>
</div>

<style is:inline>
  wa-tab-group+wa-divider {
    margin-block: 1rem 3rem;
  }
</style>
</Layout>
